*=============================================================================
* R1-3 ROBUSTNESS CHECK (Reviewer #1 omitted-factors comment)
*
* Adds the two collected-but-omitted PERCEIVED-BENEFIT / EFFICACY items to the
* full WTA model (Model 5):
*     enhance_success  (1 = class "Definitely" improves reality; 0 = Probably/Maybe)
*     influ_future     (1 = "Solidified current commitment"; 0 = other responses)
*
* TRUST / INSTITUTIONAL-CONFIDENCE and RISK / BEHAVIORAL measures were NOT
* collected in the instrument, so they are addressed as a LIMITATION, not added.
*
* Paste this block at the END of:
*   2025.07.08_Update_avgknowledge_NullTravelCost_WTA_3rdWage.do
* (after the section that generates enhance_success and influ_future).
* This produces the OFFICIAL numbers; a Python pre-check indicated results are
* stable and the two items are individually insignificant, but confirm here.
*=============================================================================

* Common sample = obs with both new items non-missing (keeps base vs aug comparable)
gen byte rob_samp = !missing(enhance_success, influ_future)

*---------------------------------------------------------------- OLS
regress WTA WTP_log i.DBegFarm avgknowledge_be avgknowledge_af ///
        total_travelcost edu_yrs i.d_male age_num if rob_samp, robust
eststo rob_ols_base

regress WTA WTP_log i.DBegFarm avgknowledge_be avgknowledge_af ///
        total_travelcost edu_yrs i.d_male age_num enhance_success influ_future, robust
eststo rob_ols_aug

*---------------------------------------------------------- Ordered probit
oprobit WTA WTP_log i.DBegFarm avgknowledge_be avgknowledge_af ///
        total_travelcost edu_yrs i.d_male age_num if rob_samp, robust
eststo rob_op_base

oprobit WTA WTP_log i.DBegFarm avgknowledge_be avgknowledge_af ///
        total_travelcost edu_yrs i.d_male age_num enhance_success influ_future, robust
eststo rob_op_aug

esttab rob_ols_base rob_ols_aug rob_op_base rob_op_aug, ///
        se r2 ar2 aic bic label nogaps ///
        title("R1-3 robustness: perceived-benefit items added to Model 5")

* Export a formatted table. esttab handles multiple stored estimates cleanly;
* the previous outreg2 ctitle("a","b",...) LIST caused r(198) "invalid name"
* and aborted the do-file before the diagnostics below could run.
esttab rob_ols_base rob_ols_aug rob_op_base rob_op_aug using ///
        "R1_3_robustness_perceived_benefit.rtf", replace se r2 ar2 aic bic label nogaps ///
        mtitles("OLS base" "OLS +items" "OProbit base" "OProbit +items") ///
        title("R1-3 robustness: perceived-benefit items added to Model 5")

*------------------------------------------------ Diagnostics requested in review
* Collinearity with the before/after knowledge variables
regress WTA WTP_log avgknowledge_be avgknowledge_af total_travelcost ///
        edu_yrs age_num enhance_success influ_future if rob_samp
estat vif
pwcorr avgknowledge_be avgknowledge_af enhance_success influ_future, sig

* Sample sizes / coverage
count if rob_samp
tab enhance_success, missing
tab influ_future, missing
	

* Use the following to close the log file created. Always put at the end
log close
